// Regression fixture for the generated Dart fluent-builder pattern's own
// edge cases (code-review findings on the builder-pattern-objects branch):
//
// - A field literally named `builder` used to collide with the class's own
//   static `{T}.builder()` factory (Dart puts static and instance members
//   in one shared namespace) — round 1 "fixed" this by renaming the
//   factory to `newBuilder`, but that fallback was itself unguarded: a
//   schema with BOTH a `builder` field AND a `newBuilder` field reproduced
//   the identical `conflicting_static_and_instance` error. The maintainer
//   decision (not to guard the fallback further, but to delete the static
//   factory entirely — see `cratestack-client-dart/CHANGELOG` /
//   `crates/cratestack-client-dart/src/field_view.rs`) means there is no
//   longer any static factory to collide with either field name. This
//   fixture proves both field names coexist cleanly as ordinary
//   fields/setters now that the entry point is only
//   `{T}Builder().builder(x).newBuilder(y).build()`.
// - A field literally named `build` collides with the builder's terminal
//   `build()` method — `FieldView::new` renames its *setter* to
//   `setBuild`, unrelated to the (now-removed) factory-name collision
//   above; both land on the same model here so the two shims are proven
//   not to interfere.
// - A required `Json` field's Dart type (`Object?`) is already nullable,
//   so the generated `build()` method must not emit a same-type `as
//   Object?` cast — `dart analyze --fatal-warnings` flags that as
//   `unnecessary_cast`.
// - issue #661: `tags String[]` is a scalar list field, mechanically
//   distinct from an optional/required scalar — it must build as `[]`
//   when unset (Dart no longer throws `StateError` the way it used to)
//   and it gets an `addTags(String)` append setter beside the existing
//   bulk `tags(List<String>)` setter, which keeps replacing. This fixture
//   is `generate-dart`-only (never `include_server_schema!`/
//   `include_embedded_schema!`, see the single grep hit for its name), so
//   it deliberately carries no `datasource` block — a database-backed
//   model has no SQL bind representation for a list-valued scalar field
//   and would reject `tags String[]` at parse time.
// - cratestack#663: `note String?` is a nullable (`Optional`-arity)
//   column. On `UpdateGadgetInput`, `null` is genuinely ambiguous between
//   "the caller never touched `note`" and "the caller explicitly cleared
//   it" — the one arity where a plain `!= null` check on the field's own
//   value can't tell the two apart. See `builder_edge_cases_patch_test
//   .dart` for the running proof (a real `flutter test`, not just a
//   generated-source text assertion) that the generated `UpdateGadgetInput`
//   /`UpdateGadgetInputBuilder` distinguish all three states over
//   `toWire()`.
model Gadget {
  id Int @id
  builder String
  newBuilder String
  build String
  meta Json
  tags String[]
  note String?
}
